  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math><mi>f</mi></math> be a differentiable function such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> for all <math><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>R</mi></math>. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></math>, then&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is equal to :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "Rf3VN",
      "text": "<math><mn>4</mn><msup><mrow><mi>e</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>",
